{
  "id": "plural",
  "name": "Plurals of nouns and adjectives",
  "level": "A1",
  "variety": "es-ES",
  "subtitle": "One house, two houses: after a vowel add -s (casa → casas). After a consonant add -es (ciudad → ciudades). The article and the adjective become plural too: las casas blancas.",
  "briefMarks": ["-s", "-es", "z → ces", "los", "las"],
  "source": "icanspeak Spanish original text (grammar-a1 run, 2026-11-04)",
  "concept": {
    "flow": [
      { "text": "los / las", "variant": "prep" },
      { "text": "noun + -s / -es", "variant": "verb" },
      { "text": "adjective + -s / -es", "variant": "verb" }
    ],
    "exampleHtml": "casa → casa<span class=\"vp-verb\">s</span> · ciudad → ciudad<span class=\"vp-verb\">es</span> · lápiz → lápi<span class=\"vp-verb\">ces</span> · el piso nuevo → <span class=\"vp-prep\">los</span> piso<span class=\"vp-verb\">s</span> nuevo<span class=\"vp-verb\">s</span>",
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "After a <strong>vowel</strong>, add <strong>-s</strong>: <em>libro → libros, calle → calles, silla → sillas</em>.",
        "tag": "Vowel: -s"
      },
      {
        "html": "After a <strong>consonant</strong>, add <strong>-es</strong>: <em>ciudad → ciudades, hospital → hospitales, mes → meses</em>.",
        "tag": "Consonant: -es"
      },
      {
        "html": "A final <strong>-z</strong> changes to <strong>-ces</strong>: <em>lápiz → lápices, luz → luces, vez → veces</em>.",
        "tag": "z → ces"
      },
      {
        "html": "Written accents can appear or go away, because the stress stays on the same sound: <em>canción → canciones, autobús → autobuses, joven → jóvenes, examen → exámenes</em>.",
        "tag": "Accents"
      },
      {
        "html": "Everything around the noun changes too: <em><strong>la</strong> casa blanc<strong>a</strong> → <strong>las</strong> casas blanc<strong>as</strong></em>. A group of men and women takes the masculine: <em>los vecinos</em> can be men and women.",
        "tag": "Agreement"
      },
      {
        "html": "Words that end in an unstressed vowel + <strong>-s</strong> do not change. Only the article shows the plural: <em>el lunes → los lunes, la crisis → las crisis</em>.",
        "tag": "No change"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>lápizes</em> → ✓ <em>lápices</em>. ✗ <em>jovenes</em> → ✓ <em>jóvenes</em>. ✗ <em>canciónes</em> → ✓ <em>canciones</em>. ✗ <em>los casas</em> → ✓ <em>las casas</em>. More on adjectives: <a href=\"/adjective-agreement\">Adjectives: agreement and position</a>.",
    "reference": {
      "showLabel": "Show overview ▼",
      "hideLabel": "Hide overview ▲",
      "tables": [
        {
          "caption": "How to make the plural",
          "head": ["The word ends in", "Rule", "Examples"],
          "rows": [
            ["a vowel", "+ -s", "casa → casas, coche → coches"],
            ["a consonant", "+ -es", "ciudad → ciudades, mujer → mujeres"],
            ["-z", "z → ces", "luz → luces, vez → veces"],
            ["-ción, -sión", "+ -es, no accent", "estación → estaciones"],
            ["unstressed vowel + -s", "no change", "el lunes → los lunes"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Accents that appear or go away",
          "head": ["Singular", "Plural"],
          "rows": [
            ["joven", "jóvenes"],
            ["examen", "exámenes"],
            ["canción", "canciones"],
            ["autobús", "autobuses"],
            ["alemán", "alemanes"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "caption": "The whole group changes",
          "head": ["Singular", "Plural"],
          "rows": [
            ["el piso nuevo", "los pisos nuevos"],
            ["la casa blanca", "las casas blancas"],
            ["un vecino amable", "unos vecinos amables"],
            ["una calle tranquila", "unas calles tranquilas"]
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  },
